Direct action by the sensitizer alone (A) cannot account for the data, because the sensitizer level is unchanged between the two probes while labeling efficiency tracks the ease of one-electron oxidation/H-atom loss on the probe itself. Option C (methyl (E)-4-oxo-4-(prop-2-yn-1-ylamino)but-2-enoate) arises from purely thermal ring opening and would therefore produce identical labeling in light and dark controls, eliminating any photo-specific difference; its formation is also independent of the phenolic versus benzyl-alcohol substitution. Carbene (D) is not generated by these structures, and Cy5-azide (E) is introduced after irradiation. Consequently the residual wavelength- and probe-dependent increment continues to isolate trace phenoxyl-radical generation as the species responsible.}
